# Rank 1819 / CVE-2026-28815 (CWE-125): apple/swift-crypto's BoringSSL-backed
# X-Wing private key decapsulates an attacker-supplied HPKE ciphertext without
# first checking its length. OpenSSLXWingPrivateKeyImpl.Backing.decapsulate(_:)
# (Sources/Crypto/KEM/BoringSSL/XWing_boring.swift at fix parent fa308c0) takes
# `encapsulated: Data` straight from the KEM/HPKE entry points, opens it with
# `withUnsafeBytes`, and passes `encapsulatedSecretBytes.baseAddress` as the
# `ciphertext` parameter of CCryptoBoringSSL_XWING_decap -- a C function whose
# header (Sources/CCryptoBoringSSL/include/CCryptoBoringSSL_xwing.h:91)
# declares `const uint8_t ciphertext[XWING_CIPHERTEXT_BYTES]` (1120) with no
# length parameter, so the callee reads 1120 bytes regardless of what the
# sender sent. A truncated encapsulated key reads past the buffer. Fix
# bb4ba815 adds `guard encapsulated.count == Int(XWING_CIPHERTEXT_BYTES) else
# { throw CryptoKitError.incorrectParameterSize }` before the call, exactly
# the guard every sibling in the same package carries: the MLKEM768
# and MLKEM1024 decapsulate(_:) implementations open with
# `guard encapsulated.count == <ciphertextByteCount> else { throw
# CryptoKitError.incorrectParameterSize }` (MLKEM_boring.swift:144/411), and
# XWing_boring.swift's own key imports guard `$0.count == XWING_PUBLIC_KEY_BYTES`
# and `ptr.count == Int(XWING_PRIVATE_KEY_BYTES) + Int(XWING_PUBLIC_KEY_BYTES)`
# before touching baseAddress -- those three throw
# CryptoKitError.incorrectKeySize, the package's error case for a wrong-sized
# *key*; the fix introduces the file's first *parameter*-size rejection. The
# pool row is correct: the vulnerable shape is present at the parent, the
# remediation is present at the fixed revision, and the merge commit's
# combined diff reads in full.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked, both stacked reasons still standing.
#
# First, an extraction gap, fixed in the companion commit: `try S` in
# statement position lowered to nothing, so the whole decapsulate body
# contributed no nodes. `vyql query -call XWING_decap` now returns the call
# node at XWing_boring.swift:241 on the parent (and `withUnsafeBytes` at
# :240), so the calls extract; the same query returns zero nodes on the fixed
# revision, because the fix also respelled `try SymmetricKey(...)` as
# `return try SymmetricKey(...)` and a return-wrapped trailing closure still
# drops its body. That asymmetry is an artifact of the fixing commit's own
# spelling and is not usable as a discriminator.
#
# Second, no binding can discriminate the guard, so no detection ships. The
# full findings view, union over three `--cache off` runs per revision
# (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB) over Sources/Crypto: 24 findings at the parent
# and the identical 24 at the fix, fingerprint sets byte-identical -- every
# one VYQL-DOS-040 on a `fatalError`/`preconditionFailure` site in an
# unrelated file (ECDSA, HMAC, the ASN1 types, DHKEM, MLKEM_wrapper), none in
# XWing_boring.swift. `vyql match` on XWing_boring.swift labels nothing at
# either revision, and the whole-tree scan (1419 findings) reports nothing on
# any KEM file but those same assertion reviews.
#
# The scoping routes are dead, re-measured at this tip. A throwaway
# `presenceNode where node.scope == "function"` binding labels zero nodes in
# any .swift file: Swift still emits one module-context node per file and
# never populates FuncDef.ContextTokens, so every context clause is file-wide
# co-presence (the rank-1792 attribution gap). A call-anchored negation does
# not even compile -- `containsAny(node.context.identifier, ...)` on a
# callExpr binding is rejected at load with "not implemented in scanner IR
# lowering". And stmt's branch lowering still gates the condition on
# `n.Kind() == "if_statement"` (swift.go:320), so the fix's
# `guard encapsulated.count == ...` contributes no node at all: the C
# analogue of the missing count-to-call correlation is filed at rank 1676.
#
# The one route the first pass left untested, now measured: a module-scope
# co-presence binding -- decap callee present, negated on the file mentioning
# `incorrectParameterSize`. On the real pair it reads 1 (XWing_boring.swift:1)
# at the parent and 0 at the fix, and on the fix re-spelled without the
# `return` (so the decap call extracts) it still reads 0, which proves the
# negation rather than the extraction accident does the work. It is nonetheless
# the fixing commit's own vocabulary, not the presence of a length check: the
# identical guard throwing CryptoKitError.incorrectKeySize -- the error case
# this file already uses for its three key-size guards -- leaves it firing at
# 1, and so does `precondition(encapsulated.count ==
# Int(XWING_CIPHERTEXT_BYTES))`. Two genuinely-enforcing variants flagged is
# the rejected shape, so the route is declined. Had it discriminated, the
# collateral was already cheap: across 475 Swift files on three other trees
# (swift-asn1 18, swift-nio 309, swift-corelibs-foundation 148) the probe
# adds nothing.
#
# What the weakness needs is "encapsulated.count compares to the ciphertext
# size in this function, at the call immediately above" -- per-function
# context facts for Swift (rank 1792), guard/if condition lowering beyond the
# first term (rank 1217), and a buffer-count-to-call correlation no frontend
# offers (rank 1676). Named, not re-filed.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap; cases 1 and 2 (the shipped
# VYQL-RF-001 try-prefix isolation pair) expected, cases 3 to 6 pinned.

test "rank1819: engine gap isolated -- environment-sourced URL fetched inside a trailing closure reports"
  lang swift
  file XWingProbe.swift
  expect VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  import Foundation

  func handler(encapsulated: Data) {
      let u = ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment["URL"]!
      encapsulated.withUnsafeBytes { raw in
          URL(string: u)
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1819: engine gap isolated -- the identical call in the identical closure, prefixed with try, reports the same"
  lang swift
  file XWingProbeTry.swift
  expect VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  import Foundation

  func handler(encapsulated: Data) throws {
      let u = ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment["URL"]!
      try encapsulated.withUnsafeBytes { raw in
          URL(string: u)
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1819: X-Wing decapsulation hands the encapsulated key's baseAddress to the fixed-size native decap with no length check"
  lang swift
  file XWing_boring.swift
  reject VYQL-MEM-064
  code
  ```
  import Foundation

  enum CryptoKitError: Error {
      case incorrectParameterSize
      case internalBoringSSLError()
  }

  struct SymmetricKey {
      init(unsafeUninitializedCapacity: Int, _ body: (inout UnsafeMutableRawBufferPointer, inout Int) throws -> Void) throws {}
  }

  struct XWING_private_key {}

  func CCryptoBoringSSL_XWING_decap(_ out: UnsafeMutableRawPointer, _ ciphertext: UnsafeRawPointer, _ key: UnsafeMutablePointer<XWING_private_key>) -> CInt { 1 }

  struct OpenSSLXWingPrivateKeyImpl {
      var privateKey: XWING_private_key

      func decapsulate(_ encapsulated: Data) throws -> SymmetricKey {
          try SymmetricKey(unsafeUninitializedCapacity: 32) { sharedSecretBytes, count in
              try encapsulated.withUnsafeBytes { encapsulatedSecretBytes in
                  let rc = CCryptoBoringSSL_XWING_decap(
                      sharedSecretBytes.baseAddress,
                      encapsulatedSecretBytes.baseAddress,
                      &self.privateKey
                  )
                  guard rc == 1 else {
                      throw CryptoKitError.internalBoringSSLError()
                  }
                  count = 32
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1819: the patched decapsulation guards the ciphertext length before opening the buffer"
  lang swift
  file XWing_boring_fixed.swift
  reject VYQL-MEM-064
  code
  ```
  import Foundation

  enum CryptoKitError: Error {
      case incorrectParameterSize
      case internalBoringSSLError()
  }

  struct SymmetricKey {
      init(unsafeUninitializedCapacity: Int, _ body: (inout UnsafeMutableRawBufferPointer, inout Int) throws -> Void) throws {}
  }

  struct XWING_private_key {}

  func CCryptoBoringSSL_XWING_decap(_ out: UnsafeMutableRawPointer, _ ciphertext: UnsafeRawPointer, _ key: UnsafeMutablePointer<XWING_private_key>) -> CInt { 1 }

  let XWING_CIPHERTEXT_BYTES = 1120

  struct OpenSSLXWingPrivateKeyImpl {
      var privateKey: XWING_private_key

      func decapsulate(_ encapsulated: Data) throws -> SymmetricKey {
          guard encapsulated.count == Int(XWING_CIPHERTEXT_BYTES) else {
              throw CryptoKitError.incorrectParameterSize
          }

          return try SymmetricKey(unsafeUninitializedCapacity: 32) { sharedSecretBytes, count in
              try encapsulated.withUnsafeBytes { encapsulatedSecretBytes in
                  let rc = CCryptoBoringSSL_XWING_decap(
                      sharedSecretBytes.baseAddress,
                      encapsulatedSecretBytes.baseAddress,
                      &self.privateKey
                  )
                  guard rc == 1 else {
                      throw CryptoKitError.internalBoringSSLError()
                  }
                  count = 32
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1819: the same guard throwing the key-size error case is equally enforcing and must not be flagged"
  lang swift
  file XWing_boring_fixed_keysize.swift
  reject VYQL-MEM-064
  code
  ```
